To generate an automatic table of contents (TOC) in a LaTeX document, you can use the `toc` package and the `\tableofcontents` command. Here's an example:

1. Add the `toc` package to the preamble of your LaTeX document:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{toc}
\begin{document}
```

2. Add the `\tableofcontents` command at the beginning of your document, after the `\begin{document}` command. This will generate the table of contents based on the section headings in your document:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{toc}
\begin{document}
\tableofcontents
```

3. Use section headings (e.g., `\section{Section 1}`) to structure your document. The TOC will automatically include these section headings.

4. If you want to customize the appearance of the TOC, you can use the `toc` package's options. For example, to change the font size, you can use:

```latex
\usepackage[fontsize=12pt]{toc}
```

5. If you want to change the format of the TOC, you can use the `toc` package's `tocstyle` option, along with the `tocloft` package. Here's an example to change the font, spacing, and numbering format:

```latex
\usepackage{tocloft}
\usepackage[titles,subfigure,hyperref]{tocstyle}
\renewcommand{\cftsecfont}{\normalfont}
\renewcommand{\cftsubsecfont}{\normalfont}
\renewcommand{\cftsecleader}{\cftdotfill{\cftsecdotsep}}
\renewcommand{\cftsubsecleader}{\cftdotfill{\cftsubsecdotsep}}
\setlength{\cftsecnumwidth}{2em}
\setlength{\cftsubsecnumwidth}{3em}
\setlength{\cftsecleader}{0cm}
\setlength{\cftsubsecleader}{0cm}
\setlength{\cftbeforesecskip}{0.5\baselineskip}
\setlength{\cftbeforesubsecskip}{0.5\baselineskip}
```

6. If you want to exclude certain sections or subsections from the TOC, you can use the `toc` package's `\addtocontents` command. For example, to exclude a section, add the following command at the end of the section:

```latex
\addtocontents{toc}{\protect\vspace{1em}}
```

This will add an empty line before the next section in the TOC.

Here's a complete example of a LaTeX document with an automatically generated TOC, using the `toc` package and the `tocloft` package to customize the TOC:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{toc}
\usepackage{tocloft}
\usepackage[titles,subfigure,hyperref]{tocstyle}

\renewcommand{\cftsecfont}{\normalfont}
\renewcommand{\cftsubsecfont}{\normalfont}
\renewcommand{\cftsecleader}{\cftdotfill{\cftsecdotsep}}
\renewcommand{\cftsubsecleader}{\cftdotfill{\cftsubsecdotsep}}
\setlength{\cftsecnumwidth}{2em}
\setlength{\cftsubsecnumwidth}{3em}
\setlength{\cftsecleader}{0cm}
\setlength{\cftsubsecleader}{0cm}
\setlength{\cftbeforesecskip}{0.5\baselineskip}
\setlength{\cftbeforesubsecskip}{0.5\baselineskip}

\begin{document}
\tableofcontents

\section{Section 1}
\addtocontents{toc}{\protect\vspace{1em}}

\subsection{Subsection 1.1}
\subsection{Subsection 1.2}

\section{Section 2}
\subsection{Subsection 2.1}
\subsection{Subsection 2.2}

\section{Section 3}
\addtocontents{toc}{\protect\vspace{1em}}
\subsection{Subsection 3.1}
\subsection{Subsection 3.2}

\end{document}
```

